CORE
main.c
--div-by-zero-check
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[worker\.division-by-zero\.1\] line 8 division by zero in 10 / divisor: FAILURE$
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line 19 before any thread: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line 26 after the spawn: UNKNOWN$
^\[bystander\.assertion\.1\] line 14 bystander: UNKNOWN$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
A refuted fatal assertion (here: undefined behaviour) in one thread makes
proven properties in all threads UNKNOWN, including code that does not follow
it in the control-flow graph: the bystander thread and the code of main after
the spawn. Code that runs before any thread starts keeps its status.
